IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ita-types`

-- Income Tax Act 1947 — PARTS 12 TO 15: WITHHOLDING, CREDITS AND PERSONS
-- CHARGEABLE.
--
-- Part 12 (withholding of tax from payments to non-residents, ss 45-45J),
-- Part 13 (s 46, tax deducted is a credit), Part 14 (double taxation relief,
-- ss 49-50C), Part 15 (persons chargeable, ss 51-60).
--
-- Source: ../source/ITA1947.txt lines 28619-29934.

§ `Parts 12 to 15 — withholding and credits`

§§ `Withholding rates (ss 45-45H)`

DECLARE `Payment to a non-resident` IS ONE OF
    `interest to an individual or Hindu joint family`          -- s 45(1)(a)(i): 24%
    `interest to any other person`                             -- s 45(1)(a)(ii): 17%
    `interest or s 12(6) payment within s 43(3)`               -- s 45(1)(a)(iii), 43(3): 15%
    `royalty or s 12(7)(a)-(b) payment within s 43(3A)`        -- s 45A, 43(3A): 10%
    `management or technical fee, s 12(7), to a non-individual` -- s 45A, 43(1)(a) via (a)(ii): 17%
    `director's remuneration to a non-resident director`       -- s 45B: 24%
    `consideration for real property disposed of by a non-resident trader`  -- s 45D: 15%
    `professional income of a non-resident individual or foreign firm`      -- s 45F, 43(4): 15% of gross
    `income of a non-resident public entertainer`              -- s 45GA, 40A: 15%
    `commission to a licensed international market agent`     -- s 45H: 3%

-- s 45(1)(a): "(i) where the person to be paid is an individual or a Hindu joint
-- family, at the rate of 24%; (ii) where the person to be paid is any other
-- person, at the rate of 17%; or (iii) where section 43(3) or (3A) is applicable
-- ..., at the rate specified in that provision". s 45B(2): 24% for directors'
-- remuneration. s 45D(1): 15% of the consideration for real property. s 45H:
-- 3%. (1C): rules may substitute a rate; (2)(b) the Comptroller may direct a
-- different rate — inputs where they apply.
@ref ss 45(1)(a), 45A, 45B(2), 45D(1), 45F, 45GA, 45H
GIVEN p IS A `Payment to a non-resident`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the withholding rate on` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `interest to an individual or Hindu joint family`          THEN 24%
    WHEN `interest to any other person`                             THEN 17%
    WHEN `interest or s 12(6) payment within s 43(3)`               THEN 15%
    WHEN `royalty or s 12(7)(a)-(b) payment within s 43(3A)`        THEN 10%
    WHEN `management or technical fee, s 12(7), to a non-individual` THEN 17%
    WHEN `director's remuneration to a non-resident director`       THEN 24%
    WHEN `consideration for real property disposed of by a non-resident trader` THEN 15%
    WHEN `professional income of a non-resident individual or foreign firm`      THEN 15%
    WHEN `income of a non-resident public entertainer`              THEN 15%
    WHEN `commission to a licensed international market agent`     THEN 3%

-- s 45(1)(b), (4)(a): the tax withheld is paid "by the 15th day of the second
-- month following the month in which the interest ... is paid".
@ref s 45(4)(a)
GIVEN `paid on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay over tax withheld from a payment on` `paid on` MEANS
    YMD (DATE_YEAR `two months on`) (DATE_MONTH `two months on`) 15
    WHERE
        `two months on` MEANS `add months` (YMD (DATE_YEAR `paid on`) (DATE_MONTH `paid on`) 1) 2

-- s 45(4): if not paid by that date, "(a) ... a sum equal to 5% of such amount
-- of tax is payable; and (b) within 30 days after the time specified in
-- paragraph (a), an additional penalty of 1% of such amount of tax is payable
-- for each completed month that the tax remains unpaid, but the total additional
-- penalty under this paragraph must not exceed 15% of the amount of tax
-- outstanding." FORK I6: (b)'s completed months are counted from the end of the
-- 30 days after the due date.
@ref s 45(4)
GIVEN tax        IS A NUMBER
      `due date` IS A DATE
      `as at`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the late withholding penalty on` tax `due on` `due date` `, as at` `as at` MEANS
    IF `as at` AT MOST `due date` THEN 0 ELSE tax TIMES 5% PLUS `additional`
    WHERE
        `start` MEANS `due date` PLUS 30
        `months` MEANS `count from` 0
        `count from` n MEANS IF `add months` `start` (n PLUS 1) AT MOST `as at` THEN `count from` (n PLUS 1) ELSE n
        `uncapped` MEANS IF `as at` GREATER THAN `start` THEN tax TIMES 1% TIMES `months` ELSE 0
        `additional` MEANS IF `uncapped` GREATER THAN tax TIMES 15% THEN tax TIMES 15% ELSE `uncapped`

-- s 45(5): failing to give notice of tax deducted by the due date is an offence:
-- "a penalty equal to 3 times the amount of tax so deducted" and "a fine not
-- exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or
-- ... both". (6): at least 6 months' imprisonment on a third or later
-- conviction of an individual.
DECLARE `Withholding offence penalty` HAS
    `penalty`                 IS A NUMBER
    `maximum fine`            IS A NUMBER
    `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `minimum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 45(5), (6)
GIVEN `tax deducted`          IS A NUMBER
      `previous convictions`  IS A NUMBER
      `an individual`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Withholding offence penalty`
`the penalty for not notifying tax deducted of` `tax deducted` `, previous convictions` `previous convictions` `, individual:` `an individual` MEANS
    `Withholding offence penalty` WITH
        `penalty`                        IS 3 TIMES `tax deducted`
        `maximum fine`                   IS 10000
        `maximum imprisonment in months` IS 36
        `minimum imprisonment in months` IS IF `an individual` AND `previous convictions` AT LEAST 2 THEN 6 ELSE 0

-- s 45(9): no withholding on interest from qualifying debt securities issued
-- 27 February 1999 to 31 December 2028, on qualifying project debt securities
-- issued 1 November 2006 to 31 December 2025, or on interest paid from
-- 21 February 2014 to a Singapore branch of a foreign company.
DECLARE `Withholding exception` IS ONE OF
    `interest from qualifying debt securities`
    `interest from qualifying project debt securities`
    `interest to a Singapore branch of a foreign company`
    `none`

@ref s 45(9)
GIVEN e          IS A `Withholding exception`
      `the date`  IS A DATE    -- of issue, or of the liability to pay for the branch case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `withholding is excepted for` e `, dated` `the date` IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `interest from qualifying debt securities` THEN `the date` AT LEAST YMD 1999 2 27 AND `the date` AT MOST YMD 2028 12 31
    WHEN `interest from qualifying project debt securities` THEN `the date` AT LEAST YMD 2006 11 1 AND `the date` AT MOST YMD 2025 12 31
    WHEN `interest to a Singapore branch of a foreign company` THEN `the date` AT LEAST YMD 2014 2 21
    WHEN `none` THEN FALSE

§§ `Foreign tax credits (ss 50, 50A, 50C)`

-- s 50(2): the credit reduces the tax on that income, but only for a person
-- resident in Singapore that year. (3): it "must not exceed the amount which would
-- be produced by computing the amount of the income ... and then charging it to
-- income tax at a rate ascertained by dividing the income tax chargeable (before
-- allowance of credit ...) on the assessable income ... by the amount of the
-- person's assessable income". (4): all the credits together not more than the
-- tax payable (excluding s 45 tax).
@ref s 50(2), (3)
GIVEN `foreign tax`           IS A NUMBER
      `the foreign income`    IS A NUMBER
      `tax before credits`    IS A NUMBER
      `assessable income`     IS A NUMBER
      resident                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the foreign tax credit for foreign tax of` `foreign tax` `on income of` `the foreign income` `, tax before credits` `tax before credits` `, assessable income` `assessable income` `, resident:` resident MEANS
    IF   (NOT resident) OR `assessable income` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `foreign tax` LESS THAN `the limit` THEN `foreign tax` ELSE `the limit`
    WHERE
        `the limit` MEANS `the foreign income` TIMES `tax before credits` DIVIDED BY `assessable income`

-- s 50C(2), (4): a pooled credit for YA 2012 on, where tax was paid abroad on
-- each elected income, the foreign headline rate was at least 15%, and the
-- Singapore tax on it is not nil: "the lower of — (a) the aggregate of the
-- income tax chargeable ... on all the elected income; and (b) the aggregate of
-- the taxes paid on all the elected income" abroad.
@ref s 50C(2), (4), (5)
GIVEN `elected income`        IS A NUMBER
      `foreign taxes paid`    IS A NUMBER
      `tax before credits`    IS A NUMBER
      `assessable income`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the pooled foreign tax credit on elected income of` `elected income` `, foreign taxes` `foreign taxes paid` `, tax before credits` `tax before credits` `, assessable income` `assessable income` MEANS
    IF `foreign taxes paid` LESS THAN `the Singapore tax` THEN `foreign taxes paid` ELSE `the Singapore tax`
    WHERE
        `the Singapore tax` MEANS IF `assessable income` EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE `elected income` TIMES `tax before credits` DIVIDED BY `assessable income`

-- s 50(4): the total of all credits "must not exceed the total income tax
-- payable by the person for that year of assessment, excluding any tax payable by
-- the person under section 45".
@ref s 50(4)
GIVEN credits IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `tax payable, excluding s 45 tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total foreign tax credits allowed, credits` credits `, tax payable` `tax payable, excluding s 45 tax` MEANS
    IF sum credits GREATER THAN `tax payable, excluding s 45 tax` THEN `tax payable, excluding s 45 tax` ELSE sum credits

§§ `Persons chargeable (ss 51-60)`

-- s 51(1): "The income of a married woman must ... be charged in her own name."
-- s 52: a trustee or guardian of an incapacitated person is chargeable as that
-- person would be. s 53: a non-resident is chargeable in the name of an agent,
-- branch or manager. s 58: a deceased person's liability passes to the executor.
-- s 60: joint trustees are jointly and severally liable.
DECLARE `Kind of chargeable person` IS ONE OF
    `the person in their own name`
    `the trustee, guardian or committee of an incapacitated person`
    `the agent, branch or manager of a non-resident`
    `the executor of a deceased person`
    `joint trustees, jointly and severally`

@ref ss 51-53, 58, 60
GIVEN `incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `non-resident acting through an agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `deceased`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `held by joint trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Kind of chargeable person`
`who is charged, incapacitated:` `incapacitated` `, non-resident with agent:` `non-resident acting through an agent` `, deceased:` `deceased` `, joint trustees:` `held by joint trustees` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `deceased`                               THEN `the executor of a deceased person`
           IF `held by joint trustees`                 THEN `joint trustees, jointly and severally`
           IF `incapacitated`                          THEN `the trustee, guardian or committee of an incapacitated person`
           IF `non-resident acting through an agent`   THEN `the agent, branch or manager of a non-resident`
           OTHERWISE `the person in their own name`
